<title>USA: Merck can market Fosamax for osteoporosis. [CORRECTED 15:28 GMT]</title>
<headline>Merck can market Fosamax for osteoporosis. [CORRECTED 15:28 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>WEST POINT, Pa. 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Merck &amp; Co Inc said the U.S. Food and Drug Administration formally approved Merck's drug Fosamax to prevent osteoporosis in postmenopausal women. (Corrects approved to treat osteoporosis).</p>
<p>Fosamax was also cleared to prevent fractures in postmenopausal women with osteoporosis, the company said.</p>
<p>The action comes after an FDA advisory committee unanimously recommended the action in February.</p>
</text>
